      "updatedAt": 1789751130830
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-763282a3-8f18-4f5b-be80-5495b6b6e793",
      "conversationId": "conv-7142e384-9819-4974-80aa-ab6f2eed4fbf",
      "role": "bot",
      "text": "# Wiki\n\n## Definition\nA **wiki** is a collaborative website or platform that allows users to create, edit, and manage content collectively through a web browser. The core principle is **open collaboration** — anyone (or authorized users) can contribute and modify content directly.\n\n## Key Characteristics\n\n| Feature | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Collaborative Editing** | Multiple users can edit pages simultaneously or asynchronously |\n| **Version History** | All changes are tracked, allowing rollback to previous versions |\n| **Hyperlinking** | Pages are interconnected through wiki-links, creating a knowledge graph |\n| **Simple Markup** | Content is typically created using lightweight formatting (not full HTML) |\n| **Access Control** | Ranges from fully open (public) to restricted (private/enterprise) |\n\n## Brief History\n- **1995** — Ward Cunningham created the first wiki, **WikiWikiWeb**, for the Portland Pattern Repository. The term \"wiki\" comes from the Hawaiian word meaning *\"quick.\"*\n- **2001** — **Wikipedia** launched, becoming the largest and most well-known wiki in existence.\n- **2000s–present** — Wikis evolved into enterprise tools (Confluence, Notion, MediaWiki deployments) and knowledge management systems.\n\n## Notable Wiki Platforms\n\n- **Wikipedia** — The largest public wiki, a free encyclopedia with 60+ million articles across 300+ languages.\n- **MediaWiki** — Open-source wiki software powering Wikipedia and many other wikis.\n- **Confluence** — Atlassian's enterprise wiki for team documentation.\n- **Notion** — A modern all-in-one workspace blending wiki, database, and project management features.\n- **Fandom (formerly Wikia)** — Hosting community-driven wikis for pop culture, gaming, and more.\n- **GitBook / BookStack** — Developer-oriented and self-hosted wiki solutions.\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n1. **Knowledge Bases** — Internal company documentation, FAQs, SOPs\n2. **Collaborative Research** — Academic teams sharing references and notes\n3. **Community Encyclopedias** — Fan wikis, open-source project docs\n4. **Project Management** — Sprint planning, requirement tracking\n5. **Education** — Classroom collaboration, shared learning resources\n\n## Pros & Cons\n\n| ✅ Advantages | ⚠️ Challenges |\n|---|---|\n| Easy to create and edit | Vulnerability to vandalism or inaccurate edits |\n| Rapid knowledge sharing | Quality control can be difficult at scale |\n| Centralized information | Information architecture can degrade without maintenance |\n| Transparent version history | Privacy/confidentiality requires careful access management |\n\n---\n\nIf you'd like me to **create a wiki document**, **set up a wiki structure** for a specific topic, or **compare wiki platforms** for your use case, just let me know.",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 1,
      "createdAt": 1789751130844,
      "updatedAt": 1789751130844
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-5784a498-7670-4586-8228-0d6a8218de03",
      "conversationId": "conv-7142e384-9819-4974-80aa-ab6f2eed4fbf",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "hi",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 2,
      "createdAt": 1789751130853,
      "updatedAt": 1789751130853
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-b14a5e50-946b-48d8-8700-3391cccb9be8",
      "conversationId": "conv-7142e384-9819-4974-80aa-ab6f2eed4fbf",
      "role": "bot",
      "text": "Hello! I'm ZyroChat, your professional AI workspace assistant. I can help with:\n\n- **Chat & research** — Answer questions, gather information, brainstorm ideas\n- **Writing & documents** — Create, edit, or organize content\n- **Coding** — Write, debug, or architect software solutions\n- **File & data analysis** — Process and understand your datasets\n- **Project productivity** — Manage workflows and plan initiatives\n\nWhat would you like to tackle today?",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 3,
      "createdAt": 1789751130867,
      "updatedAt": 1789751130867
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-dd546a7e-23da-4e34-9202-71fa7f05829f",
      "conversationId": "conv-7142e384-9819-4974-80aa-ab6f2eed4fbf",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "can you create a project",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 4,
      "createdAt": 1789751130879,
      "updatedAt": 1789751130879
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-0f1338ee-8ef4-43f7-8b3a-e49665364bd5",
      "conversationId": "conv-7142e384-9819-4974-80aa-ab6f2eed4fbf",
      "role": "bot",
      "text": "# Project Creation\n\nI can absolutely help. To give you the most useful output, I need a bit more context:\n\n## What kind of project?\n\n| Type | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **Software** | Web app, CLI tool, API, library, mobile app |\n| **Document / Plan** | Project charter, roadmap, PRD, spec doc |\n| **Structure / Scaffold** | Folder hierarchy, config files, starter templates |\n| **Data / Analysis** | Pipeline, notebook, dashboard |\n\n## To get started, tell me:\n\n1. **Goal** — What is the project supposed to do or deliver?\n2. **Tech / Format** (if applicable) — e.g., Python, TypeScript, Markdown, Figma-style wireframe\n3. **Scope** — MVP / full build / just the scaffolding\n4. **Constraints** — Deadline, team size, existing codebase\n\n---\n\n### Quick example\n\nIf you said:\n\n> *\"Create a Python CLI tool that parses CSV files and outputs a summary report.\"*\n\nI'd deliver:\n\n- Folder structure\n- `main.py` with working logic\n- `requirements.txt`\n- `README.md` with usage instructions\n\n---\n\nWhat are you building? Give me the details and I'll scaffold it.Here are some starter templates I can generate for you right now:\n\n### 🚀 Ready-to-Run Scaffolds\n\n**1. Python Project**\n```\nmy-project/\n├── src/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   └── main.py\n├── tests/\n├── requirements.txt\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\n**2. Node.js / TypeScript Web App**\n```\nmy-app/\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.ts\n│   ├── routes/\n│   └── controllers/\n├── public/\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n├── .env.example\n└── README.md\n```\n\n**3. HTML/CSS/JS Landing Page**\n```\nlanding-page/\n├── index.html\n├── css/\n│   └── styles.css\n├── js/\n│   └── app.js\n└── assets/\n    └── images/\n```\n\n**4. Markdown Project Documentation**\n```\nproject-docs/\n├── README.md\n├── PRD.md\n├── roadmap.md\n├── changelog.md\n└── diagrams/\n```\n\n---\n\n### What I need from you:\n\n- **Pick a template above** or describe something custom\n- **Name your project**\n- **Specify any features** — authentication, database, API endpoints, UI components\n\nI'll generate the full file contents, ready to copy and run. Just say the word.",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 5,
      "createdAt": 1789751130897,
      "updatedAt": 1789751130897
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-0a7df0a8-8792-464a-8d32-b15660fafe40",
      "conversationId": "conv-d5215f6e-bab6-4325-8c7e-3023783cfffa",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Hello AI",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 0,
      "createdAt": 1789802347978,
      "updatedAt": 1789802347978
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-f77b3466-3fca-4cb0-b633-ca3da63ada44",
      "conversationId": "conv-d5215f6e-bab6-4325-8c7e-3023783cfffa",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "Hello! How can I help?",
      "sources": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "index": 1,
      "createdAt": 1789802347982,
      "updatedAt": 1789802347982
    },
    {
      "id": "mess-c5f06385-4c1a-43a4-a507-f8f649d146f1",
      "conversationId": "conv-ae2e9ef4-a5a9-4dba-8271-a7888dd98bd1",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Hello AI",
      "sources": [],
